    "description": "Frances Hodgson Burnett’s novel follows Mary Lennox from a neglected colonial childhood into the locked rooms and winter grounds of Misselthwaite Manor, where curiosity, friendship, honest conflict, and the patient revival of a hidden garden transform Mary, her cousin Colin, and Colin’s grieving father.",
